Several posters comment on the difficulty, nay, impossibility of the game.
It is tough, now - tough enough to force one into hacking the game rather
than playing it.  Oh, I see, a *feature* :-)

One way to satisfy several different levels of players is to have different
levels of the game with presently configurable parameters different for
each one.  Easier levels could have probabilities of shops increased,
certain very nasty monsters excluded, probabilities of good objects
increased and generally correspond to hard undefined.  Each game difficulty
level could correspond to its own score file.  Experts would quickly tire
of the easier versions and move on to the expert level while those hack
and slash twits like myself will no doubt stay at easier levels.

The present discover mode is an excellent tool and helps some, but if
you are sufficiently weak, you will never kill the current monster and
will constantly have to ask to not die.  The three levels of difficulty
in Dark Castle give fumble fingered people like myself a starting chance.

